+# Project Specification: Pulseboard
+
+**Project ID**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-11  
+**Status**: Specified  
+**Play level**: Build  
+**Archetype**: b2b_saas
+
+## Sources
+
+- **Primary input**: `brief.md` — Pulseboard brief.
+- **Known facts**: Team facilitators lose action items after weekly meetings; the product extracts proposed items from an uploaded transcript and requires confirmation of owner and due date before a reminder can be scheduled; the pilot is five teams; reviewed-proposal and overdue-action targets are specified; it is not a meeting recorder, calendar replacement, or autonomous message sender; email versus Slack reminders is unresolved.
+- **Inferences**:
+  - [INFERENCE] A small web product for five teams is appropriately specified at the Build play level and as a B2B SaaS product; the brief does not establish enterprise or platform-wide scope.
+  - [INFERENCE] Facilitators need a reviewable action-item list because the stated problem is loss of actions after weekly meetings.
+
+## Project overview
+
+Pulseboard helps team facilitators turn a weekly meeting transcript into proposed follow-up actions without allowing unreviewed automation. A facilitator uploads a transcript, reviews each proposed action, and confirms its owner and due date before any reminder can be scheduled. The product is bounded to post-meeting action follow-through for a five-team pilot; it does not record meetings, replace calendars, or send messages autonomously.
+
+## Vision and goals
+
+**Vision**: Every action proposed in a weekly meeting becomes an owned, time-bound commitment that the team can follow through on.
+
+1. **Reviewed proposed actions**: At least 80% of proposed action items are reviewed during the pilot.
+2. **Fewer unowned overdue actions**: Reduce unowned overdue actions by 30% after four weeks.
+
+## PROFILE surfaces
+
+| Surface | Adapter | Target | Source of truth | Required by |
+|---------|---------|--------|-----------------|-------------|
+| Root README | `readme` | `README.md` | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/project.md#project-overview` | UX-RC / API-RC |
+
+## Users and jobs
+
+### Primary user
+
+- **User**: Team facilitator.
+- **Situation**: After a weekly meeting with an available transcript.
+- **Problem**: Proposed action items are lost, leaving overdue actions without an owner.
+- **Core job**: Turn proposed meeting actions into confirmed, owned, due-dated follow-up commitments.
+- **Desired outcome**: Action items have been reviewed and, where appropriate, have a confirmed owner and due date before a reminder can be scheduled.
+
+### Other affected users
+
+- **Team members who own actions**: Receive follow-up only after a facilitator has confirmed the action's owner and due date.
+
+### Current alternatives
+
+- **Facilitator-managed meeting follow-up**: Can capture actions manually, but does not prevent action items from being lost or remaining unowned after weekly meetings.
+
+## Success measures
+
+| Measure | Baseline | Target | Horizon | How measured |
+|---------|----------|--------|---------|--------------|
+| Proposed action-item review rate | To establish during the five-team pilot | At least 80% of proposed items reviewed | During the pilot | Ratio of reviewed proposed action items to all proposed action items |
+| Unowned overdue actions | To establish at pilot start | 30% reduction | Four weeks | Compare the count of unowned overdue actions at pilot start and after four weeks |
+
+## Commercial intent
+
+- **Commercial posture**: Not stated.
+- **Buyer / payer**: [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Who, if anyone, buys or pays for Pulseboard?]
+- **Value exchanged**: [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: What commercial value or funding arrangement applies?]
+- **Revenue model or funding constraint**: [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Is the five-team pilot paid, internally funded, or otherwise funded?]
+- **Unit constraint**: Not stated.
+
+## Definition of done
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a meeting transcript, review proposed action items, and confirm an owner and due date before a reminder can be scheduled.
+- [ ] At least 80% of proposed action items can be observed as reviewed during the pilot.
+- [ ] The change in unowned overdue actions can be measured over four weeks.
+- [ ] Meeting recording, calendar replacement, and autonomous message sending remain excluded.
+- [ ] The reminder delivery channel is resolved without preselecting email or Slack.
+
+## Scope
+
+### In scope
+
+- Uploading a meeting transcript.
+- Extracting proposed action items from the uploaded transcript.
+- Facilitator review of proposed action items.
+- Confirming an owner and due date before a reminder can be scheduled.
+- Scheduling a reminder after the required confirmation.
+- A pilot with five teams.
+
+### Out of scope
+
+- Meeting recording.
+- Calendar replacement.
+- Autonomous message sending.
+
+### Later only
+
+None named.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- **Business**: Pilot with five teams.
+- **User/trust**: A facilitator must confirm both an owner and due date before any reminder can be scheduled; messages must not be sent autonomously.
+- **Technical facts already fixed**: The product is a web product. No provider, architecture, or reminder channel is fixed.
+
+## Risks and assumptions
+
+### Risks
+
+- **Proposed action extraction may not produce items facilitators consider useful**: The review rate target could be missed; test early with pilot transcripts and observe review behavior.
+- **The unresolved reminder channel may not fit the pilot teams' workflow**: Scheduling may not lead to effective follow-through; determine the appropriate channel before implementing delivery.
+- **The four-week measurement may lack a usable baseline**: The reduction target could not be evaluated; establish the baseline at pilot start.
+
+### Assumptions
+
+- **Facilitators can provide an uploaded transcript after weekly meetings**: Disproved if pilot teams cannot or will not supply transcripts.
+- **Requiring a confirmed owner and due date reduces unowned overdue actions**: Disproved if the four-week comparison does not show the intended reduction.
+- **Five pilot teams provide enough usage to measure the stated review rate**: Disproved if insufficient proposed action items are generated or reviewed.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Should scheduled reminders be delivered by email or Slack?
+- What commercial posture, buyer or payer, and funding model apply to the five-team pilot?
+- What constitutes an "overdue action" for the baseline and four-week comparison?
+- What happens to a proposed action item that a facilitator decides not to confirm?
+
